exports[`screen: 'help partner webhooks create' > en 120 plain 1`] = `
"  bladecp partner webhooks create
 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Adds an HTTPS address that receives the events you choose. The signing secret shows only once:
  store it in your system to check the BladeCP-Signature header of each delivery against the exact
  body.

  Usage ──────────────────────────────────────
  bladecp partner webhooks create --url <url> --event <type>... [--name <name>]

  Options ────────────────────────────────────
  --url <url>      Address that receives the events (https)
  --event <type>   Event type to send (repeat it, or separate with commas)
  --name <name>    A name to tell the endpoint apart (for example Production WHMCS)

  Event types: provision.created, provision.status.changed, provision.suspended,
  provision.unsuspended, provision.terminated, invoice.paid, invoice.failed, subscription.upgraded,
  subscription.downgraded, vibe.account.activated, vibe.account.plan_changed,
  vibe.account.suspended, vibe.account.reactivated, vibe.account.terminated.
  Each event has a stable ID. A delivery can arrive more than once, so your system should skip an
  ID it already processed.

  Examples ───────────────────────────────────
  › bladecp partner webhooks create --url https://billing.example.com/bladecp --event invoice.paid --event
    provision.created --name "Production WHMCS"
    send paid invoices and new services to your billing system

  Global options ─────────────────────────────
  --json                 Print machine-readable JSON (no colors, no prompts)
  --api-url <url>        API address (default https://api.bladecp.com)
  --lang <en|pt-BR|es>   Language for messages
  --debug                Describe each request on stderr (the key is never shown)
  --verbose              Same as --debug
  -h, --help             Show help
  -v, --version          Show the version

  See also  bladecp partner webhooks rotate-secret <endpoint>"
`;

